# Stands in for the firmware's own QML module, which lives at /ebrmain/qml on
# the reader and exists nowhere else — it is armel, and it is the reason the
# screens cannot be run on a host at all without this directory.
#
# Only what the app actually uses is here: three singletons, the text element
# every label is built on, the header and one checkbox. The numbers are the
# ones measured on a PB629, so a layout test is checking against the geometry
# the device really has.
module com.pocketbook.controls

singleton Global 1.0 Global.qml
singleton GlobalValues 1.0 GlobalValues.qml
# FontStyles is not here: its members are Heading2, BodyS and the like, and a
# QML property name may not begin with a capital. It is set as a context
# property from main.cpp instead, which has no such rule.

StyledText 1.0 StyledText.qml
AppHeader 1.0 AppHeader.qml
CheckBox 1.0 CheckBox.qml
